      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the value of \\( n \\) for which the four-digit number \\( 712n \\) (with units digit \\( n \\)) is divisible by 18, we need to ensure that \\( 712n \\) is divisible by both 2 and 9 (since \\( 18 = 2 \\times 9 \\)).\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n#### 1. Divisibility by 2:\nA number is divisible by 2 if its last digit is even. Therefore, \\( n \\) must be one of the even digits: 0, 2, 4, 6, or 8.\n\n#### 2. Divisibility by 9:\nA number is divisible by 9 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 9. The sum of the digits of \\( 712n \\) is:\n\\[\n7 + 1 + 2 + n\n\\]\nCombine these to form:\n\\[\n10 + n\n\\]\n\n#### 3. Finding \\( n \\) such that \\( 10 + n \\) is divisible by 9:\nLet’s test each even digit for \\( n \\):\n\n- If \\( n = 0 \\):\n  \\[\n  10 + 0 = 10 \\quad (\\text{not divisible by 9})\n  \\]\n\n- If \\( n = 2 \\):\n  \\[\n  10 + 2 = 12 \\quad (\\text{not divisible by 9})\n  \\]\n\n- If \\( n = 4 \\):\n  \\[\n  10 + 4 = 14 \\quad (\\text{not divisible by 9})\n  \\]\n\n- If \\( n = 6 \\):\n  \\[\n  10 + 6 = 16 \\quad (\\text{not divisible by 9})\n  \\]\n\n- If \\( n = 8 \\):\n  \\[\n  10 + 8 = 18 \\quad (\\text{divisible by 9})\n  \\]\n\nThus, \\( n = 8 \\) makes the sum of the digits divisible by 9.\n\n#### Verification:\nWhen \\( n = 8 \\):\nThe number becomes \\( 7128 \\). We check:\n- It is clearly divisible by 2 (since its last digit is 8).\n- The sum of the digits is \\( 7 + 1 + 2 + 8 = 18 \\), which is divisible by 9.\n\nTherefore, \\( 7128 \\) meets the criteria for divisibility by 18.\n\n### Final Answer:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
